{"id": "tea:yogavimsika:1", "source": "src:yogavimsika", "location": {"ref": "1", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "All religious activity is yoga, because it joins one to liberation; but here [yoga] is especially that concerned with posture and the rest.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "terms": ["trm:yoga"], "concepts": ["cpt:yogavimsika-five-yogas"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogavimsika:19-20", "source": "src:yogavimsika", "location": {"ref": "19-20", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Supportless yoga is meditation on the formless perfected soul; it leads to omniscience and then to the highest liberation, where the cessation of all yoga (ayoga) is reached.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:analambana-yoga"], "concepts": ["cpt:yogavimsika-five-yogas"], "paths": ["pth:yogavimsika-five-yogas"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogavimsika:2", "source": "src:yogavimsika", "location": {"ref": "2", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "In the teaching this [yoga] is fivefold: posture (sthāna), sound (ūrṇa), meaning (artha), support (ālambana) and the supportless; two of these are yoga of action, three yoga of knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "terms": ["trm:alambana", "trm:analambana-yoga"], "concepts": ["cpt:yogavimsika-five-yogas"], "paths": ["pth:yogavimsika-five-yogas"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
